              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Mandarin for a position in a firm, then the Mandarin for to get promoted."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: guǎnlǐ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "guǎnlǐ — \"to manage; to be in charge of\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "tā guǎnlǐ yì jiā fàndiàn — She manages a restaurant."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its characters come later; for now it is a word for the ear."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two third tones meet in this word: guǎn is said with a rising tone before lǐ, and the spelling keeps both marks."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "guǎnlǐ is built from guǎn 'to be in charge' and 理 'to put in order', both inherited from Middle Chinese, kwanX and liX (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'a pipe (a wind instrument)' and 'to be in charge', and the second 'to work jade' and 'a pattern'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying how it was."
            }
          ]
        },
